WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.680
So as I grew up there, yes, I did form a
community, but I think for me,

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:07.020
there was always something within that
made me feel out of place.

3
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:13.760
Like... Hi, everyone. My name is Mitchell
Barure.

4
00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:20.040
I was basically born in Zimbabwe, and I
grew up in South Africa.

5
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.040
[Rewind sound effect, then music]
[On-screen text: "The background story..."]

6
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.300
One of my favorite quotes by Nelson
Mandela says, "Let your decisions

7
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:31.600
reflect your hopes and not your fears."
And that is exactly how I mustered

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:37.060
up the courage to travel from South Africa
to Zimbabwe, to Ethiopia,

9
00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:42.880
and finally to Kigali, Rwanda, to study at
the African Leadership University.

10
00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:49.000
In terms of

11
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.900
how I grew up, I basically grew up a bit
in Zimbabwe, and then the rest

12
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.900
of my life afterwards, my entire high
school and a bit of my primary

13
00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:57.700
school, was done in South Africa.

14
00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:01.780
So as I grew up there, yes, I did form a
community, but I think for me,

15
00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.100
there was always something within that
made me feel out of place.

16
00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:08.700
Like, this isn't my home. It's a temporary
place that I'm staying in.

17
00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:12.700
And I'd always think, like, why can't I go
back to Zimbabwe and stay

18
00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:15.540
there? Because that's my home. That's
where I'd feel most comfortable.

19
00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:17.600
That's not how I felt in South Africa.

20
00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:21.620
So I think that probably sparked something
in me that, OK, why can't

21
00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:25.040
we stay in Zimbabwe? And now you look at
Zimbabwe, you can see there's

22
00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.920
a bad economic state, bad governance.

23
00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:31.320
Everything is just terrible in terms of
supply to water.

24
00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:34.220
People can't even get water running
through their taps.

25
00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:36.200
And it's just a lot that just goes on.

26
00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:40.300
And I think that's something that is
influencing the mission that I will

27
00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.760
probably have. I'm looking towards how we
can make Zimbabwe a better

28
00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:47.080
place, so that all the Zimbabweans can
actually come back home and not

29
00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:53.640
have to leave the country. In 2023,

30
00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:58.100
we discovered that my younger sister
Marcia's tonsils were swelling up

31
00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:02.640
and blocking her airway. In that moment, I
realized we had two options.

32
00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:07.700
We could either go to a public hospital,
but that would mean waiting

33
00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:12.340
in a long queue and having no guarantee of
actually seeing a doctor and

34
00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:14.180
receiving a solution in the same day.

35
00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:18.460
Our second option would be to go to a
private hospital that can be accessed

36
00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:22.620
through a health insurance, or paying cash
at that moment.

37
00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:26.320
And that would mean that you would pay an
excessively large amount just

38
00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:30.080
to receive a consultation, and then pay
another excessively large amount

39
00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:35.060
to get the solution. Then I thought to
myself, as an African individual

40
00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:40.000
who may not know about health insurance or
cannot access a private hospital,

41
00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:43.100
what would happen in such a dire
situation?

42
00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:46.260
And that is where my mission comes in.

43
00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:50.940
My mission is to increase the quality of
health care systems in Zimbabwean

44
00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:55.640
communities, as well as to increase the
accessibility to health care

45
00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:58.820
for all individuals living in Zimbabwean
communities.

46
00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:04.480
I hope to develop a model that can be
applied all over Africa and other

47
00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:06.980
communities that are facing the same
situation.

48
00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:11.400
I know that in order to see the Zimbabwe
that I desire to see, that is

49
00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.960
transformed, I cannot do that by myself.

50
00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:17.900
But I am looking forward towards
collaborating with other individuals

51
00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:23.020
that have different missions that will aim
towards transforming Zimbabwe

52
00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:25.100
and Africa as a whole.

53
00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:33.100
[Music]
